{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/835804-are-you-prepared-in-case-of-emergencies","id":835804,"title":"Are you prepared?(In case of Emergencies)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-23T08:55:28-08:00","id":835804,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon4.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Are you prepared?(In case of Emergencies)","content":"Assume an event that disrupts one or more of the following:<ul><li>Power</li> <li>Water</li> <li>Local food distribution</li> <li>Cable/internet/ cell system</li> </ul>Do you have a way to get news if the cable/internet/ cell system is down?<br /> Do you have a battery powered broadcast radio or TV?<br /> Do you have 2 week supply of canned or dried goods at home if you need to shelter in place?<br /> Do you have jugs of water?<br /> Do you have a way of dealing without power?<br /> Do you have an alternate form of mid to long range communications if the cell system is down?<br /> Do you have a go bag?<br /> Do you have a stash of cash in case ATMs or the card reader at the Gas pump isn't working?<br /> <br /> My background:<br /> I went thru Hurricanes David &amp; Fredrick in Puerto Rico. I've seen Mesocyclones and dust storms up close and personal in Houston. Was caught between buildings when the squall line of the &quot;wall of Black &quot;tornado hit.<br /> <br /> Licensed Amateur radio operator who has helped out in a some incident command situations.<br /> <br /> So let's discuss planning for an emergency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","user":"Chattnos","date":". 02-23-2016, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T15:31:02-08:00","id":836060,"title":"","content":"For water I keep a couple flats of bottled water in the garage (bearing in mind I live in California), and keep a couple lifestraws in the emergency kit as well as chlorine. I'm not that far from a river, which is remarkably fault-tolerant as a water supply.<br /> <br /> For Power/Updates I keep a crank/battery powered radio and generally have batteries about the place.<br /> <br /> Food is probably the biggest weak spot, as I have only a pantry filled with canned food products plus of course the deep freeze. In the event of a distribution problem I've got enough to cover the household for probably a couple weeks to a month if I start a lot of cooking (before stuff spoils).<br /> <br /> I don't bother with a Go bag because my background is growing up in the boonies of Canada, where the disasters are ice storms, wind storms that take out power. In a disaster you stay put and wait it out a week or two. If a disaster is so hard core that basic functionality can't be restored after 2 weeks, then odds are cash isn't going to be worth a whole hell of a lot.<br /> <br /> As for dealing without power, we'd lack the ability to communicate out electronically, but that would also be the case if cell/internet goes down. That's not too terrible in itself, as we'd be hunkered down reading books to pass time, not playing social butterflies.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T17:14:45-08:00","id":836111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/835804-are-you-prepared-in-case-of-emergencies?p=836060#post836060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For water I keep a couple flats of bottled water in the garage (bearing in mind I live in California), and keep a couple lifestraws in the emergency kit as well as chlorine. I'm not that far from a river, which is remarkably fault-tolerant as a water supply.<br /> <br /> For Power/Updates I keep a crank/battery powered radio and generally have batteries about the place.<br /> <br /> Food is probably the biggest weak spot, as I have only a pantry filled with canned food products plus of course the deep freeze. In the event of a distribution problem I've got enough to cover the household for probably a couple weeks to a month if I start a lot of cooking (before stuff spoils).<br /> <br /> I don't bother with a Go bag because my background is growing up in the boonies of Canada, where the disasters are ice storms, wind storms that take out power. In a disaster you stay put and wait it out a week or two. If a disaster is so hard core that basic functionality can't be restored after 2 weeks, then odds are cash isn't going to be worth a whole hell of a lot.<br /> <br /> As for dealing without power, we'd lack the ability to communicate out electronically, but that would also be the case if cell/internet goes down. That's not too terrible in itself, as we'd be hunkered down reading books to pass time, not playing social butterflies.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like you have good set up. I don't buy bottled water I use 2 liter soda bottles(or jugs of similar plastic) filled from tap. I may throw a drop of iodine in.<br /> I stay away milk jugs as as they are gas permeable. <br /> <br /> You say you don't need a go bag. I curious what you would in case of wild fire or gas leak. In my case I have worry about a nuke site up the road. I also may have to worry about chemical as I'm near a rail yard.<br /> <br /> We are ok on food for about two weeks need to pickup a 40 or 50lb bag of Beans and Rice.<br /> Need to upgrade my water supplies. I do have a roof catch.<br /> <br /> I have some ham radios in the house(UHF, VHF, HF) and everyone is licensed and knows how use them.<br /> <br /> I'm lacking on pet supplies and bug out plan for them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T05:58:33-08:00","id":836376,"title":"","content":"My situation is very dependant on where I'm living at the time.<br /> <br /> Usually I'm in Paris. Small appartment, not much place to have anything that's not immediatly usefull. If the water supply is out or the power goes down, I have... maybe three to four days water, about two weeks food. I do have a bag with cash in case of emergency, but otherwise that's about it. My best bet would be to grab a bike and get out into the countryside. On the other hand, anything that can overwhelm the multiple redundancies inherent to the infrastructure of the capital would probably be enough to get me in a few days anyway, so...<br /> <br /> When I'm at my parent's place, on a small island in the pacific ocean (New Caledonia), it's another matter entirely. There are cyclones to watch out for, and we usually have at least a tropical depression each year. So there's enough water for a week at least, maybe two if we get some time to prepare. Gas bottles and solar panels for power, a good amount of food. I can probably hold on from a week to a month depending on how many people there are and the season. If we need to move, we have a sailboat (with a radio and enough place for four people) and we can just go off and live off the land and sea for a while. I've actually lasted a month out at sea with no supplies before with my brother for the hell of it (fishing, picking up coconuts and fruits on islands and replenishing the water supplies of the boat by just finding a clean stream and walking up to where it's nice enough to drink from it). I don't know how long I could last if there was a medical emergency in that case, but barring that, I like to think I could probably live for years, hopping from island to island. Even better if there's some way for me to scrounge up ammo and I've brought a gun with me, cause that means I can also hunt when on the shore (deers, wild pigs, fat pigeons and bats all would make for a good addition to fish, fruits, tarot and the occasionnal vegetable.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":541,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","user":"LeTipex","date":". 02-24-2016, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T08:32:22-08:00","id":836427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/835804-are-you-prepared-in-case-of-emergencies?p=836376#post836376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My situation is very dependant on where I'm living at the time.<br /> <br /> Usually I'm in Paris. Small appartment, not much place to have anything that's not immediatly usefull. If the water supply is out or the power goes down, I have... maybe three to four days water, about two weeks food. I do have a bag with cash in case of emergency, but otherwise that's about it. My best bet would be to grab a bike and get out into the countryside. On the other hand, anything that can overwhelm the multiple redundancies inherent to the infrastructure of the capital would probably be enough to get me in a few days anyway, so...<br /> <br /> When I'm at my parent's place, on a small island in the pacific ocean (New Caledonia), it's another matter entirely. There are cyclones to watch out for, and we usually have at least a tropical depression each year. So there's enough water for a week at least, maybe two if we get some time to prepare. Gas bottles and solar panels for power, a good amount of food. I can probably hold on from a week to a month depending on how many people there are and the season. If we need to move, we have a sailboat (with a radio and enough place for four people) and we can just go off and live off the land and sea for a while. I've actually lasted a month out at sea with no supplies before with my brother for the hell of it (fishing, picking up coconuts and fruits on islands and replenishing the water supplies of the boat by just finding a clean stream and walking up to where it's nice enough to drink from it). I don't know how long I could last if there was a medical emergency in that case, but barring that, I like to think I could probably live for years, hopping from island to island. Even better if there's some way for me to scrounge up ammo and I've brought a gun with me, cause that means I can also hunt when on the shore (deers, wild pigs, fat pigeons and bats all would make for a good addition to fish, fruits, tarot and the occasionnal vegetable.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting the differences. I did not know about New Caledonia. Cyclones are a regional name for tornados here(US). Possibly archaic. What you call a Cyclone and your neighbors to the north call a typhoon, we call a Hurricane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T10:01:15-08:00","id":836500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/835804-are-you-prepared-in-case-of-emergencies?p=836111#post836111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You say you don't need a go bag. I curious what you would in case of wild fire or gas leak. In my case I have worry about a nuke site up the road. I also may have to worry about chemical as I'm near a rail yard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in an urban area so don't have a huge amount of worry about wild fires. Also having lived through several I know that if they do start sweeping in to my region, it's not a short-notice situation. I'll have several hours to depart, if not several days notice.<br /> <br /> as for gas leaks... if you're talking a localized (to the house) gas leak, it's easy, turn off the main, vent the house, get the pipe fixed, end of problem. If it's a neighborhood gas main, the problem is larger but the solution is still the same... it's california, so living without gas for a few weeks is at most a minor irritation rather than an actual problem.<br /> <br /> As for a natural gas leak, there are no major well sites nearby, and california in general isn't noted for sour gas wells, so I'm fairly unconcerned on that side of things. <br /> <br /> I *am* downstream from a dam, but when house hunting I made sure I was at least a moderate distance off even the worst-case dam breaking flood areas. So that would at most be annoying as it would cut off bridges and shut down some roads I use ever few weeks but again, fairly minor overall.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T20:42:44-07:00","id":876229,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately other than whats in the fridge/freezer and back up freezer, i don't have much in prepper style food or the like.. And seeing how things are going, i DO feel more people need to get into the prepping trend, otherwise when the fit hits the shan, a LOT of people are going to be up the creek without a paddle..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T18:27:25-07:00","id":878298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/835804-are-you-prepared-in-case-of-emergencies?p=876229#post876229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately other than whats in the fridge/freezer and back up freezer, i don't have much in prepper style food or the like.. And seeing how things are going, i DO feel more people need to get into the prepping trend, otherwise when the fit hits the shan, a LOT of people are going to be up the creek without a paddle..</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T20:30:42-07:00","id":878391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/835804-are-you-prepared-in-case-of-emergencies#post835804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assume an event that disrupts one or more of the following:<ul><li>Power</li> <li>Water</li> <li>Local food distribution</li> <li>Cable/internet/ cell system</li> </ul>Do you have a way to get news if the cable/internet/ cell system is down?<br /> Do you have a battery powered broadcast radio or TV?<br /> Do you have 2 week supply of canned or dried goods at home if you need to shelter in place?<br /> Do you have jugs of water?<br /> Do you have a way of dealing without power?<br /> Do you have an alternate form of mid to long range communications if the cell system is down?<br /> Do you have a go bag?<br /> Do you have a stash of cash in case ATMs or the card reader at the Gas pump isn't working?<br /> <br /> My background:<br /> I went thru Hurricanes David &amp; Fredrick in Puerto Rico. I've seen Mesocyclones and dust storms up close and personal in Houston. Was caught between buildings when the squall line of the &quot;wall of Black &quot;tornado hit.<br /> <br /> Licensed Amateur radio operator who has helped out in a some incident command situations.<br /> <br /> So let's discuss planning for an emergency.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Do you have a way to get news if the cable/internet/ cell system is down?</b><br /> always good to have a transistor radio<br /> <b>Do you have 2 week supply of canned or dried goods at home if you need to shelter in place?</b><br /> I barely have a 2 week supply of my anti-anxiety medication, I never have any food in the house but in the event that we suffer some crazy disaster and anime girl figures become currency I'll be rich AF<br /> <b>Do you have jugs of water?</b><br /> yup<br /> <b>Do you have a way of dealing without power?</b><br /> We used to get hit with tons of hurricanes in North Carolina so we all just throw parties, we don't buy food or water or batteries, we buy beer and liquor.<br /> <b>Do you have an alternate form of mid to long range communications if the cell system is down?</b><br /> I can yell really loudly. <br /> <b>Do you have a go bag?</b><br /> 3 day supply one aside from tools but yes.<br /> <b>Do you have a stash of cash in case ATMs or the card reader at the Gas pump isn't working?</b><br /> I've been on medical leave for almost 2 months, the only thing I've got a stash of is bills I can't afford and currently hiding from.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T21:01:55-07:00","id":878419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/835804-are-you-prepared-in-case-of-emergencies?p=878298#post878298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>With the US debt being at 19 Tril and counting, its only going to be a matter of time before WE are like Greece, and in economic dire straits, and when that happens imo the social unrest WOULD cause the Fit to hit the Shan.<br /> Just look at how large a percentage of the US population depends ON those government hand outs. Now what happens when all that goes away?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:46:49-07:00","id":955816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/835804-are-you-prepared-in-case-of-emergencies?p=878419#post878419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the US debt being at 19 Tril and counting, its only going to be a matter of time before WE are like Greece, and in economic dire straits, and when that happens imo the social unrest WOULD cause the Fit to hit the Shan.<br /> Just look at how large a percentage of the US population depends ON those government hand outs. Now what happens when all that goes away?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Greece and US are not comparable. Apples and Oranges situation.<br /> Greece has no control over its currency and foolishly joined a confederation.<br /> We have control of our currency and are a federation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T13:44:01-07:00","id":955860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/835804-are-you-prepared-in-case-of-emergencies#post835804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assume an event that disrupts one or more of the following:<ul><li>Power</li> <li>Water</li> <li>Local food distribution</li> <li>Cable/internet/ cell system</li> </ul>Do you have a way to get news if the cable/internet/ cell system is down?<br /> Do you have a battery powered broadcast radio or TV?<br /> Do you have 2 week supply of canned or dried goods at home if you need to shelter in place?<br /> Do you have jugs of water?<br /> Do you have a way of dealing without power?<br /> Do you have an alternate form of mid to long range communications if the cell system is down?<br /> Do you have a go bag?<br /> Do you have a stash of cash in case ATMs or the card reader at the Gas pump isn't working?<br /> <br /> My background:<br /> I went thru Hurricanes David &amp; Fredrick in Puerto Rico. I've seen Mesocyclones and dust storms up close and personal in Houston. Was caught between buildings when the squall line of the &quot;wall of Black &quot;tornado hit.<br /> <br /> Licensed Amateur radio operator who has helped out in a some incident command situations.<br /> <br /> So let's discuss planning for an emergency.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. I have crank radio and my grandfathers ham radio<br /> 2. Yea I have ruffly 2 months worth of food stored for 6 people. I'm trying to get up to 9 months per person.<br /> 3. Yea I ave lots of water stored and a few ways to gather rain and clean river water. <br /> 4. I have a generator and I'm working on getting a solar set up. <br /> 5. Same as 1.<br /> 6. Not anymore. I need to create a new one because the bag I was using for the old one broke. <br /> 7. Yes<br /> <br /> I like planing for survival situations. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T14:35:42-07:00","id":955897,"title":"","content":"If/when i get more flush in funds, i will start looking into doing more prepping..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"